{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"],"title":"Reference"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" is a domain plugin that owns a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsState"},{"type":"text","text":" slice, fetches a JSON wire format via a provider-agnostic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsService"},{"type":"text","text":", and answers reads against state. Bucketing is pure FNV-1a so reads are synchronous and offline-capable."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Three flag types from one wire format:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"boolean"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — on\/off with rollout percentage (0–100)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"variant"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — string-typed weighted variants for A\/B tests."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"value"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — typed remote-tunable scalar ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bool"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For end-to-end wiring, see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Library-target","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Library target"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Product: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Import: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxFeatureFlags"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Wire-format","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Wire format"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"json","code":["{","  \"version\": 1,","  \"flags\": {","    \"new_onboarding\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"rollout\": 25 },","    \"checkout_layout\": {","      \"type\": \"variant\",","      \"variants\": [","        { \"value\": \"control\", \"weight\": 50 },","        { \"value\": \"treatment\", \"weight\": 50 }","      ]","    },","    \"max_free_uploads\": { \"type\": \"value\", \"value\": 5 }","  }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin rejects unknown "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":" values and falls back to the last-known-good cache. Defaults always live in Swift at the call site — this keeps them type-checked and forces “what if missing?” thinking."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Bucketing-and-identity","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Bucketing and identity"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bucket = FNV1a(bucketingID + \":\" + flagKey) % 100"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stable per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(bucketingID, flagKey)"},{"type":"text","text":" pair forever."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Same input always produces the same bucket."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Per-flag."}]},{"type":"text","text":" A user isn’t always in the “early” group across different flags."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Identity resolution."}]},{"type":"text","text":" When a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userIDKeyPath"},{"type":"text","text":" is configured "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the current user ID is non-nil, that is used. Otherwise the install ID is used. Anonymous users get a stable per-install identity; logged-in users get stable cross-device assignment. A user’s variant "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"can"}]},{"type":"text","text":" shift once at login — acceptable for nearly all real use cases."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"FNV-1a was chosen because it’s simple, dependency-free, and matches GrowthBook’s algorithm so apps migrating from GrowthBook get compatible buckets."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Evaluation-order","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Evaluation order"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For each read, in priority:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Local override present?"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Return it."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Flag in remote config?"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Evaluate (rollout \/ variant assignment \/ value lookup)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Otherwise"}]},{"type":"text","text":" return the Swift-side default."}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"anchor":"Persistence","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Persistence"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Install ID"}]},{"type":"text","text":" persisted to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" on first generation. Read at hydration via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsState.hydrated(from:defaultConfig:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Last-known config"}]},{"type":"text","text":" persisted after every successful refresh. Hydrates as fallback before first network success."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Local overrides"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" persisted by default. Restart = clean state."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"exposedKeys"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" persisted. New session = fresh exposure events."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Exposure-tracking","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Exposure tracking"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A\/B testing is only analytically valid if you know which users actually saw each variant — bucketing alone is insufficient because the code path branching on the flag might never execute."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["store.send(.featureFlags(.recordExposure(key: \"checkout_layout\")))"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Or via the SwiftUI sugar:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["WizardView()","    .recordsExposure(of: .checkoutLayout, store: store, action: AppAction.featureFlags)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin dedupes per session and fires the optional "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onExposure"},{"type":"text","text":" callback (passed at plugin init). Wire that callback to your analytics plugin to forward exposures as events."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Refresh-policy","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Refresh policy"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public enum RefreshPolicy: Sendable {","    case manual                                      \/\/ every .refresh fetches","    case automatic(minInterval: TimeInterval)        \/\/ debounce; default 300s","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apps dispatch "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refresh"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"App.scenePhase"},{"type":"text","text":" transitions; the plugin’s debouncing makes this safe to call frequently. The plugin does not subscribe to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIApplication"},{"type":"text","text":" notifications — wiring stays in the host app."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Service-protocol","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Service protocol"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol FeatureFlagsService: Sendable {","    func fetch() async throws -> FeatureFlagsConfig","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One method. Caching, hydration, evaluation all live in the plugin."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Built-in-HTTPFeatureFlagsService","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Built-in: `HTTPFeatureFlagsService`"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"JSONDecoder"},{"type":"text","text":". Apps host their JSON anywhere — static file on a CDN, Cloudflare Worker, their own server. Zero backend infrastructure required."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Third-party adapters (LaunchDarkly, GrowthBook, Statsig) conform to the same protocol without changing the plugin."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Typed-flag-keys","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Typed flag keys"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public struct BoolFlag: Sendable, Hashable","public struct VariantFlag<Variant: RawRepresentable & Sendable> where Variant.RawValue == String","public struct ValueFlag<Value: Sendable>"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read API on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsState"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["state.isEnabled(.newOnboarding, default: false)","state.variant(of: .checkoutLayout)","state.value(of: .maxFreeUploads)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reads are pure synchronous functions. Per-property observation works as it does for any other state slice — views re-render only when the flag they read changes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Action-semantics-selected","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Action semantics (selected)"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshSucceeded(FeatureFlagsConfig, fetchedAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is dispatched on every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refresh"},{"type":"text","text":" (including debounced refreshes that return an unchanged config). Consume config transitions by observing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsState"},{"type":"text","text":" or a value derived from it — not by mapping this action. See "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture#Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","ab